                <pb facs="ve_d7-1" n="1" xml:id="ve_d7-1"/>

                <head>VE–7. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On March 24, 1958, in a <hi rendition="#italic">Supplementary Report</hi> to the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Report of the President’s Special Committee to
                        Investigate Crude Oil Imports</hi>, dated July 29, 1957, the Special
                    Committee recommended additional restrictions on crude oil imports quotas for
                    Districts I–IV, the area east of the Rocky Mountains. The President approved the
                    Special Committee’s report in a memorandum dated March 25, 1958, and in similar
                    memoranda released on June 4, July 1, and December 23, 1958, the President
                    approved the Special Committee’s recommendations relating to 1) importation of
                    petroleum products other than crude, 2) allocations for District V, the Pacific
                    West Coast, and 3) continuance of existing crude oil allocations through
                    February 28, 1959. See <hi rendition="#italic">Public Papers of the Presidents
                        of the United States</hi>: <hi rendition="#italic">Dwight D. Eisenhower, 1958</hi>
                    (Washington: 1958), p. 230. Documentation concerning U.S. oil policy is printed
                    in <ref target="frus:frus1958-60v04"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1958–1960, vol. IV, Foreign Economic Policy</ref>.
                    Further documentation is located in Department of State decimal files 411.006,
                    411.316, and 831.2553, and in ARA/EST Files, Lot 61 D 319, “Petroleum Policy” and
                    “Oil U.S. Legislation”, and ARA/EST Files, Lot 62 D 8, “Petroleum Policy” and “Oil
                    Import Program.”</p>
            </div>
